WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.970
- Well, last month you went to Houston

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.090
and reported form George Floyd's funeral.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.940
What was the most powerful moment

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.170
of that experience for you?

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.050
- Well, within a week I was in Houston,

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.540
but before that I was in Minneapolis

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.890
for the memorial service.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.350
I think the most powerful moment for me

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:19.200
was when Reverend Sharpton
was doing the eulogy

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.260
and he said, "Let's pause for
eight minutes and 46 seconds."

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.820
And I was outside the church

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.440
and I'm seeing this
sea of people out there

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.140
and just looking at the faces,
some people were crying,

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.280
some people were praying,

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.600
some people were just shellshocked.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.760
I think I was in the shellshocked category

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.690
of trying to imagine that period of time.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.170
It's a long, long time.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.770
And, of course, it references the time

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.460
that the officer's knee
was on George Floyd's neck.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.323
But I think that really moved me.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:51.984
You've seen the video,

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:54.380
but you see it through a different lens

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.290
when you really feel that length of time.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.000
- Yeah, I was gonna say,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.200
sitting there for that long,

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.950
it really puts things in perspective

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:07.570
of how long it actually
is, is what you're saying.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.270
But, you know, as a journalist,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.130
what makes Floyd's story different

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.210
from others like it that you've covered?

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.820
Because unfortunately
there's been a lot of stories

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.410
of people dying that should not have died

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.530
and/or police brutality

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.880
or just any instance that's
kind of in a similar vein.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.660
We hear about so many,
Breonna Taylor, Tamir Rice,

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.730
we hear about so many,

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.290
so what do you think
made this one different?

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.330
- I think because we were
all eye witnesses to it.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.180
You're right, we've
seen many of these cases

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.420
and very often ends up
being jumbled dash cam video

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.430
or body cam video.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.230
This was a rather steady shot

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:46.170
of a man being suffocated to death.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.640
And there's no equivocating that,

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.510
there's no walking around it,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.570
there's no, "Well, maybe it
could've been this or that."

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.230
It was what you saw

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.430
and when you bear witness
to something that awful,

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.030
you can't walk away from
it, you can't discount it,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.530
you can't leave it to other people.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.760
And so I think, you know, when I look out,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.080
and sometimes protesters come
right here by my apartment,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.070
I look out and I see black and white

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:14.483
and Asians and Hispanics, I
see a rainbow of people here,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.507
as human beings who are saying,

00:02:17.507 --> 00:02:20.370
"No, that doesn't stand in our society."

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.920
So I think his case has just,

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.110
it symbolized so many things we've seen,

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.580
but it was just so graphic and so awful

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.490
and as I said, we're
all eye witnesses to it.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.960
- Yeah, no, I agree with that.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.930
And it's on film.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.370
It's hard to negate that.

